🇺🇸🇮🇷 US Continues Striking Iranian Maritime Shipping,Iran Continues Ballistic Missile Strikes on US Bases

▪️The US has released more videos of strikes it carried out against civilian Iranian maritime  shipping;

▪️While Iran is striking back at primarily US bases in Jordan, the US military aviation striking Iranian maritime shipping is mainly from its naval presence in the region - and Iran has so far failed to strike any US ships among it;

▪️Additionally, while Iran has and is hitting US bases across the region, expected strike windows are predictable and the US is able to either send aircraft airborne or disperse them to smaller airfields across the region - part of the ACE (agile combat employment) minimizing any damage to US warplanes themselves;

▪️While airfields are damaged, it is possible to repair much of the damage done as seen in Ukraine whose airfields are constantly struck by Russian drones and missiles;

▪️Until heavier losses are suffered by specifically US military aviation and ships in its fleet, the US will maintain its ability to incrementally eliminate Iranian maritime shipping, maintain the general instability restricting energy exports from all of West Asia, enhance its energy dominance strategy worldwide, and thus maintain its war on multipolarism;

▪️If the US starts losing more aircraft and suffer even just damaged ships, this may begin to shift the equation...
